  "implemented": [
    "A distinct private flat-local-v1 production family now owns canonical framing, full chronological native admission, real source capture, writable journal and complete four-name participant. It uses the actual shared kernel and genuine shared opening/upload/final-witness machinery, not a copied owner overlay.",
    "One raw payload pool and canonical table-prefix recipes reproduce every incoming file byte for byte. The first snapshot retains its existing whole-file SHA rule; later flat files use canonical manifest identity plus verified raw payload digests. No old aggregate graph file or cumulative header is stored as an opaque payload.",
    "Original, CURRENT, PENDING and unsaved LIVE document/review histories, unique ordered versions, whole upload rows and historical provider-only pixels remain conserved. Capture appends to the actual imported input and does not flush edits, retry uploads or activate a network peer.",
    "Exact payload roles, native lane digest spellings, counts, per-role bytes and declared semantic uses are validated before native factory execution. Retained parent/journal input MIME and length also refuse early. Correct hashes alone do not establish valid native chronology or upload/pixel continuity.",
    "Genuine family identity and child tickets reserve the actual four names. Preparing/prepared/operational phases cold-reconcile aborted or lost-completion saves without reconstructing acknowledged missing owners. The live source keeps its journal/input/provider independently of the retired parent.",
    "Actual upload exclusion and native witnesses survive awaited releases, input disposal, handle closure and final callbacks. Unreturned owners and uncommitted handoff wrappers deny use. All wrappers are constructed before the last native comparison; cleanup retries the same actual owners.",
    "Fresh read execution policy and an independent Wasm instance work after the writer grant/factory retires. Exact family/intent types, nominal owners and native source selection-policy types survive complete handoff."
  ],
